---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How Reviews Work" description="How BostonVentures scores hotels and tours, and the rules every review follows.">
  <div class="wrap max-w-3xl py-12 prose-bv">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-navy">How Reviews Work</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink/50">Last updated: November 2026</p>
    <ul>
      <li>I only score a hotel or tour after I have actually stayed there or done it.</li>
      <li>Hotels are scored out of 10, in steps of 0.5, in five categories: Room, Food &amp; Drinks, Beach &amp; Pool, Activities and Service. Activities can have two scores (families and party seekers).</li>
      <li>The overall score is the average of the five, unless I explain why I set it differently.</li>
      <li>Scores are judged against the price, so every review shows the price I paid.</li>
      <li>If a hotel gives me a free or discounted stay, the page says so. A free stay never changes the scores.</li>
      <li>Hotels I have not reviewed show facts only. I never copy, rewrite or summarize guest reviews from other websites.</li>
      <li>Facts like prices and restaurant counts are checked against a source, and each page shows when they were last checked.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
